cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "mcp-scrutiny"
abstract: >-
  Static and semantic security scanner for Model Context Protocol servers. It
  answers four questions about an MCP deployment: whether anything is launched
  from a floating version, whether a tool definition changed since it was
  approved, whether a description contains instructions the model would obey,
  and whether the tools combine into a capability path no single tool should
  have. Measured against 514 public MCP servers and 12 709 tool definitions;
  the survey it produced is linked below.
authors:
  - family-names: "Tamouffe Teyo"
    given-names: "Ulrich Bryand"
    alias: "bryand410"
version: 0.1.7
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bryand410/mcp-scrutiny"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/mcp-scrutiny/"
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - security scanner
  - tool poisoning
  - prompt injection
  - supply chain
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "What 514 public MCP servers expose to the model"
    url: "https://github.com/bryand410/mcp-survey/blob/main/docs/2026-11-public-mcp-survey.md"
